<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#FiniteDoubleShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for Finite Double. Its constraints below specify the permitted values and combinations."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#FiniteDoubleShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: No automatic target; applied only when another shape references it or a caller explicitly selects it. Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#FiniteDoubleShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Finite Double Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#FiniteDoubleShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#GeoTransform> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The affine mapping from pixel/line to ground coordinates, carrying the six coefficients asref:originX, scaleX, skewX, originY, skewY, scaleY -- GDAL's GT[0..5] in that order. A north-up raster leaves both skews zero; only the skews make a rotated grid expressible."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#GeoTransform> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity; subclass links below are the asserted hierarchy, not merely similarity links."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#GeoTransformShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for asref:originX, asref:originY, asref:scaleX, asref:scaleY, asref:skewX, asref:skewY. Its constraints below specify the permitted values and combinations."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#GeoTransformShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of asref:GeoTransform; objects of asref:hasGeoTransform Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#GeoTransformShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Geo Transform Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#GeoTransformShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#GroundControlPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "One correspondence between a pixel position and a ground position. A set of these georeferences an image that no single affine can, e.g. an unrectified swath."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#GroundControlPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity; subclass links below are the asserted hierarchy, not merely similarity links."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#GroundControlPointShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for asref:gcpIdentifier, asref:gcpPixelX, asref:gcpPixelY, asref:gcpX, asref:gcpY, asref:gcpZ. Its constraints below specify the permitted values and combinations."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#GroundControlPointShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of asref:GroundControlPoint; objects of asref:hasGroundControlPoint Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#GroundControlPointShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Ground Control Point Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#GroundControlPointShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#PixelCenter> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Pixel registration referring to a sample center. This metadata does not change the normalized affine convention by itself."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#PixelCenter> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#PixelCenter> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#PixelCorner> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Pixel registration referring to a pixel corner; the normalized affine convention places the first pixel's upper-left corner at column/row zero."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#PixelCorner> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#PixelCorner> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#coordinateEpoch> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Coordinate epoch in decimal years for coordinates in a dynamic reference frame; distinct from acquisition time and CRS reference epoch."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#coordinateEpoch> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#crsIdentifier> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Authoritative CRS IRI; supports authorities and compound or vertical systems without assuming a single numeric code scheme."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#crsIdentifier> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#epsgCode> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The positive numeric code identifying a coordinate reference system in the EPSG registry; it is not a complete substitute for all CRS metadata."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#epsgCode> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#footprintWKT> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The ground area covered, as a WKT geometry in the resource's CRS -- typically a polygon of the four image corners. Formats that state corners directly rather than an affine (NITF's IGEOLO, the BLOCKA corner strings) have no scale or origin to give, so a footprint is the only georeference they carry."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#footprintWKT> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#gcpIdentifier> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The source-local identifier distinguishing a control point within its control-point set."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#gcpIdentifier> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#gcpPixelX> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Column position of the control point in the image grid."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#gcpPixelX> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#gcpPixelY> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Row position of the control point in the image grid."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#gcpPixelY> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#gcpX> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The first ground-coordinate ordinate of a control point in the declared control-point CRS."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#gcpX> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#gcpY> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The second ground-coordinate ordinate of a control point in the declared control-point CRS."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#gcpY> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#gcpZ> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Ground elevation of the control point. Optional: many formats give 2-D control only."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#gcpZ> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#groundControlPointCRS> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "CRS of the ground-control-point set, which may differ from the raster's affine CRS. No reprojection or precedence is implied."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#groundControlPointCRS> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#hasCRS> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "CRS of the resource's ground coordinates. A CRS identifier is not itself a transformation or a geometry."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#hasCRS> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#hasGeoTransform> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The complete affine transformation resource relating grid column/row coordinates to ground coordinates."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#hasGeoTransform> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#hasGroundControlPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A measured or supplied correspondence between an image-grid location and a ground coordinate."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#hasGroundControlPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#hasRationalTransform> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The rational-polynomial geolocation model associated with a resource, with its basis contract declared explicitly."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#hasRationalTransform> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#heightOffset> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Normalization offset for the height coordinate, interpreted using polynomialBasis. Scales must be strictly positive."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#heightOffset> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#heightScale> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Normalization scale for the height coordinate, interpreted using polynomialBasis. Scales must be strictly positive."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#heightScale> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#latitudeOffset> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Normalization offset for the latitude coordinate, interpreted using polynomialBasis. Scales must be strictly positive."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#latitudeOffset> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#latitudeScale> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Normalization scale for the latitude coordinate, interpreted using polynomialBasis. Scales must be strictly positive."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#latitudeScale> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#lineDenominator> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Ordered vector of 20 finite coefficients; repeated coefficient values are allowed."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#lineDenominator> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#lineNumerator> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Ordered vector of 20 finite coefficients; repeated coefficient values are allowed."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#lineNumerator> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#lineOffset> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Normalization offset for the line coordinate, interpreted using polynomialBasis. Scales must be strictly positive."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#lineOffset> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#lineScale> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Normalization scale for the line coordinate, interpreted using polynomialBasis. Scales must be strictly positive."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#lineScale> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#longitudeOffset> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Normalization offset for the longitude coordinate, interpreted using polynomialBasis. Scales must be strictly positive."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#longitudeOffset> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#longitudeScale> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Normalization scale for the longitude coordinate, interpreted using polynomialBasis. Scales must be strictly positive."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#longitudeScale> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#originLatitude> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Origin northing expressed as a GEOGRAPHIC latitude. See asref:originLongitude; the general form is asref:originY."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#originLatitude> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#originLongitude> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Origin easting expressed as a GEOGRAPHIC longitude. Use only when the CRS really is geographic; for an origin in projected units (metres, feet) use asref:originX, of which this is the geographic special case."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#originLongitude> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#originX> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Easting of the grid origin in the units of the CRS, degrees or metres alike (affine coefficient GT[0]). The general form of asref:originLongitude, which presumes a geographic CRS and is therefore wrong for the projected rasters that make up most of the corpus."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#originX> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#originY> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Northing of the grid origin in the units of the CRS (affine coefficient GT[3]). The general form of asref:originLatitude."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#originY> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#pixelRegistration> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The declared pixel reference convention. Consumers must honor the normalized transform convention rather than apply an additional shift blindly."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#pixelRegistration> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#polynomialBasis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "IRI of the complete published polynomial convention. A profile must define the ordered 20 monomials, normalized inputs, CRS/units and pixel reference. Different coefficient orderings are not interchangeable."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#polynomialBasis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#sampleDenominator> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Ordered vector of 20 finite coefficients; repeated coefficient values are allowed."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#sampleDenominator> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#sampleNumerator> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Ordered vector of 20 finite coefficients; repeated coefficient values are allowed."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#sampleNumerator> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#sampleOffset> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Normalization offset for the sample coordinate, interpreted using polynomialBasis. Scales must be strictly positive."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#sampleOffset> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#sampleScale> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Normalization scale for the sample coordinate, interpreted using polynomialBasis. Scales must be strictly positive."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#sampleScale> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#scaleX> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Ground distance per pixel along X (affine coefficient GT[1])."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#scaleX> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#scaleY> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Ground distance per pixel along Y (affine coefficient GT[5]). Conventionally NEGATIVE for a north-up raster, whose rows run southward while northings increase."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#scaleY> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#skewX> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Rotation/shear term: ground X per pixel ROW (affine coefficient GT[2]). Zero for a north-up raster. Without this and asref:skewY a rotated or sheared grid cannot be georeferenced at all, only misplaced."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#skewX> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#skewY> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Rotation/shear term: ground Y per pixel COLUMN (affine coefficient GT[4]). Zero for a north-up raster."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#skewY> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#wktString> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Coordinate reference system WKT, not WKT geometry. No equivalence to GeoSPARQL geometry serialization is asserted."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#wktString> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for coordinate references and geolocation metadata. Declare units, reference frame and pixel conventions explicitly; metadata validation does not execute coordinate transformations. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
